  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Incident Report Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is the incident report form?\", \"a\": \"An incident report form is the written record of one event at work or on site: an injury, a near miss, property damage, a theft, or a security problem. It captures when and where it happened, who was involved, the sequence of events, and the response.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you make an incident report form template?\", \"a\": \"List the incident types you track, the questions each one needs and who should hear about each report. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English. It builds an incident report form template anyone can open on a phone, with every report saved to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find free incident report forms?\", \"a\": \"Universities and template sites post blank versions, and most offer an incident report form PDF you can print. Each one was written for a single employer, and several of its fields will not fit yours. Emergent is free to start, which covers building an incident report form that messages a supervisor and keeps every report in one table.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of an incident report form?\", \"a\": \"A short example for a slip in a cafe reads like this. Date and time: Tuesday, 7:40 a.m. Location: front counter, by the drinks fridge. What happened: a customer slipped on water from a leaking fridge and caught the counter. Injuries: none reported. Witness: the barista on shift. Action taken: floor dried, sign placed, fridge repair requested.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a blank incident report form include?\", \"a\": \"A blank incident report form should include the date, time, and exact location, everyone involved, and witnesses with a way to reach them. Leave space for a plain account of events and the reporter's signature. Keep fault off the page: OSHA's incident investigation guidance warns that hunting for someone to blame stops short of the root cause.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who uses incident report forms?\", \"a\": \"Anyone who runs a site where people work, learn, or visit uses incident report forms. Hotels log guest falls, gyms record equipment injuries, and construction crews file near misses before a crane lift. Property managers note damage to units. HR and safety leads read the reports too, because a worker's injury becomes part of the employer's safety records.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a paper incident report form better than an online one?\", \"a\": \"Paper is fine for a one-off event, and online wins once reports arrive every week. An online form stamps the time, takes photos from a phone, and alerts a supervisor while the shift is still running. Paper copies wait in a tray and get retyped before anyone can count them. On Emergent, each report lands as a row in a database you own, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an employee incident report form?\", \"a\": \"An employee incident report form records an injury, illness, or near miss involving a worker on the job. Employers under OSHA's recordkeeping rule fill in the OSHA 301 Incident Report, or an equivalent, within 7 calendar days of learning of a recordable case. If someone is hurt, the supervisor pulls family details from their emergency contact form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track incident report forms?\", \"a\": \"Track them in one list that shows which reports are still open and who owns each fix. Sort that list by location and incident type every month to see where the same problem keeps coming back. When a fix needs a repair, open a work order form from the report, and maintenance gets the location and photos without retyping them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I customize an incident report form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Rename the fields, drop the ones that never apply, and add questions for the incidents you see most, such as a vehicle number for fleet crashes or a room number for hotels. In Emergent, the change is one sentence in plain English, and the form and its database table update together.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
